1	//! `CommandRunner`-shelled implementation of [`GitDataSource`], consolidated
2	//! from five independently hand-rolled `git`-subprocess fallbacks that used
3	//! to live at each call site (`callisto-graph`'s `changed.rs`, `tags.rs`,
4	//! `commands/tag.rs`, `aggregate.rs`, and `callisto-conventional`'s
5	//! `window.rs`). Every operation here is reachable purely via
6	//! [`callisto_model::CommandRunner`], so it works on every target,
7	//! including `wasm32`, where native `gix` (`GitRepository`) is entirely
8	//! unavailable.
9	//!
10	//! Callers should not construct [`ShellGit`] directly except in tests that
11	//! specifically want to exercise the shell backend in isolation; use
12	//! [`crate::GitAccess::discover`] instead, which selects between this and
13	//! the native backend automatically.
